{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["Therefore it is said — concerning these journeys that they retraced and went around the land of Edom, as written: ״וְנָסַב אֶת הַר שֵׂעִיר יָמִים רַבִּים״ — and they went back until they reached the well mentioned above. Then it would be said, in the recounting of matters, that they praised the Holy One, blessed be He, and recalled the miracles of the Sea of Reeds and the miracles performed in the wadi Arnon and at the well — ״אָז יָשִׁיר יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — now that they saw the well, for at first they did not sing over it, because then Moshe and Aharon were punished on its account." "את והב — the yahav of the Holy One, blessed be He. As in: ״הַשְׁלֵךְ עַל ה׳ יְהָבֶךָ״. And likewise from יהיה, [as in] ״מַה־יֶּהְיֶה לְאָדָם״; from יקושתי [in] ״וְגַם־נִלְכַּדְתְּ בָבֶל״, ״פֶּן־תּוּקַשׁ בּוֹ״, ״לְמַעַן תּוֹרֵא״ — vav in place of yod. So too והב from יהב."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:44.872043665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}